  "articles": [
    {
      "sequence_id": 1,
      "text": "            Spanish distinguishes between 'hay' (there is/there are) to indicate the existence of something, and 'estar' when referring to a specific object's location. \nThese drills require you to convert sentences using 'hay' (indefinite reference) into sentences with 'estar' (definite reference) while maintaining meaning. \nFor example, '¿Dónde hay un restaurante barato?' (Where is there a cheap restaurant?) becomes '¿Dónde está el restaurante barato?' (Where is the cheap restaurant?).\n"
    }
